abstract: >-
  Management Research Notes is a portable, file-based academic knowledge
  base for management and business sustainability research. Each
  peer-reviewed article becomes one Markdown note with YAML frontmatter
  (trusted bibliographic metadata, a controlled-vocabulary topic taxonomy,
  three custom analytic fields — unit_of_analysis, level_of_theory,
  dependent_variable_family — and verbatim evidence anchors on every
  factual claim) and a human-readable distillation (research question,
  mechanism, theoretical contribution, practical implication, limitations,
  future research, APA citation). A small Python pipeline derives a SQLite
  index with FTS5, a CSV export, and a BibTeX file from the notes, and a
  two-layer faithfulness audit (mechanical substring check on evidence
  anchors plus a cold-context independent auditor scoring prose fields against
  a published rubric) gates every note into the library. Version 0.52.0
  (2026-08-03) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 63 issue 1 and volume 62 issue 6 — 27 notes, all v2 augmentations.
  A backfill adds no papers, so the record total remains 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 634 v2, and 472 v3 notes. All 27 augmentations passed
  the validator and initial mechanical diff-guard without a gate failure. Each
  touched note passed a fresh full independent 9-field rubric-v2 audit, with a
  final 242 of 243 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED and one faithful PARTIAL
  accepted after four evidence-based legacy-field repairs across three notes.
  Lee's founder-succession Limitations is retained because raw extracted lines
  888–925 support the field even though the fitted audit input cuts at an
  interleaved REFERENCES heading. This is the fourth consecutive backfill batch
  run end-to-end on gpt-5.6-sol for both augmentation and audit. The recurring
  workshop cross-family spot-audit applies; the next calibration runs at the
  batch-20 review.
  Version 0.51.0
  (2026-08-02) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 63 issues 3 and 2 — 24 notes, all v2 augmentations. A backfill adds
  no papers, so the record total remains 1,167; the version-tier census shifts
  to 61 v1, 661 v2, and 445 v3 notes. All 24 augmentations passed the validator
  and initial mechanical diff-guard without a gate failure. Each touched note
  passed a fresh full independent 9-field rubric-v2 audit, with a final 215 of
  216 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED and one faithful PARTIAL accepted after
  nine evidence-based edit operations across six notes in two repair rounds
  and three audit rounds. Beckman's Future Research is retained because the
  raw extracted text supports its gender rationale, although the fitted audit
  input cuts at an interleaved REFERENCES heading. This is the third
  consecutive backfill batch run end-to-end on gpt-5.6-sol for both
  augmentation and audit. The recurring workshop cross-family spot-audit
  applies; the next calibration is due around batch 20.
  Version 0.50.0
  (2026-08-02) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 63 issues 5 and 4 — 24 notes, all v2 augmentations. A backfill adds
  no papers, so the record total remains 1,167; the version-tier census shifts
  to 61 v1, 685 v2, and 421 v3 notes. All 24 augmentations passed the validator
  and initial mechanical diff-guard without a gate failure. Each touched note
  passed a fresh full independent 9-field rubric-v2 audit, with a final 216 of
  216 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED and no residual PARTIAL, after seven
  evidence-based legacy-field repairs across four notes in one repair round
  and two audit rounds. This is the second consecutive backfill batch run
  end-to-end on gpt-5.6-sol for both augmentation and audit. The recurring
  workshop cross-family spot-audit applies; batch 16's review scored 27 of 27
  agreement.
  Version 0.49.0
  (2026-08-01) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 64 issue 1 and volume 63 issue 6 — 25 notes, all v2 augmentations.
  A backfill adds no papers, so the record total remains 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 709 v2, and 397 v3 notes. All 25 augmentation deltas
  passed the validator and mechanical diff-guard on the first attempt. Each
  touched note passed a fresh full independent 9-field rubric-v2 audit, with a
  final 225 of 225 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED and no residual PARTIAL,
  after five evidence-based legacy-field repairs across four notes in two
  repair rounds and three audit rounds. This is the first backfill batch run
  end-to-end on gpt-5.6-sol for both augmentation and audit; batches 01–07
  recorded claude-opus-4-8 and batches 08–15 recorded claude-opus-5. A
  cross-family spot-audit follows at workshop review.
  Version 0.48.0
  (2026-08-01) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 64 issue 3 and volume 64 issue 2 — 25 notes, all v2 augmentations.
  A backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the
  version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 734 v2, and 372 v3 notes. The upgrade
  phase was the cleanest of the backfill so far: all 25 augmentations passed
  the validator and the mechanical diff-guard on the first attempt, with zero
  self-fix cycles. Each touched note passed a fresh full independent 9-field
  rubric-v2 audit, and this is the first batch of the backfill to finish
  spotless — 225 of 225 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED, with no residual PARTIAL
  accepted — after nineteen evidence-based repairs across ten notes in three
  repair rounds and four audit rounds. Six of the thirteen round-1 PARTIALs were
  the no-practice-section scope drift characteristic of this 2021 cohort, in
  which 14 of the 25 papers contain no practical-implication marker at all.
  Three of the five PARTIALs surviving into round 2 were introduced by the
  repairs themselves and were caught only because every repaired note is
  re-audited.
  Version 0.47.0
  (2026-07-31) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 64 issue 5 and volume 64 issue 4 — 25 notes, all v2 augmentations.
  A backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the
  version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 759 v2, and 347 v3 notes. The upgrade
  phase was the fourth consecutive clean one, with 24 of 25 augmentations
  passing the validator and the mechanical diff-guard on the first attempt.
  Each touched note passed a fresh full independent 9-field rubric-v2 audit at
  224 of 225 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED, after seven evidence-based repairs
  across six notes in three repair rounds. All six round-1 PARTIAL verdicts fell
  on legacy prose fields written before the v3 standard and none on the three new
  v3 sections, the cleanest new-field result of the backfill so far. One PARTIAL
  is accepted and documented rather than edited: Sitzmann's Future Research is
  the interleaved-references truncation class, where the REFERENCES heading sits
  atop the second column while the first still carries body prose, so the strip
  discarded 24.6% of the paper and the flagged claim verifies in the raw text.
  A seventh repair came not from the audit but from an augmentation agent's
  flag-don't-fix report that source verification upheld against the auditor's
  own SUPPORTED verdict.
  Version 0.46.0
  (2026-07-30) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 65 issue 1 and volume 64 issue 6 — 26 notes, all v2 augmentations.
  A backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the
  version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 784 v2, and 322 v3 notes. The upgrade
  phase was the third consecutive clean one, with all 26 augmentations passing
  the validator and the mechanical diff-guard on the first attempt and no
  self-fix cycles, and each touched note passed a fresh full independent
  nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 229/234 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with
  zero UNSUPPORTED or CONTRADICTED, after twenty-one evidence-based repairs
  across sixteen notes in three repair rounds — the heaviest repair load of the
  backfill to date. Fifteen of the twenty-one repairs fell on legacy prose
  fields written before the v3 standard, and practical-implication scope drift
  was the dominant class with six instances, three of them on papers whose text
  contains no practical-implications section at all and none of the audiences
  the notes addressed. The multi-study support-pattern class recurred for a
  third consecutive batch, and one note inverted a premise outright, resting
  causal inference on an instrumental-variable model the paper concludes is
  unnecessary. Six repairs touched new v3 fields, five of them Data & Measures
  with five distinct causes, none a repeated defect. Five residual PARTIAL
  verdicts are documented rather than edited: two are the interleaved-references
  truncation class, in which a two-column REFERENCES heading sits above
  continuing Future Research prose so the strip discards it and the flagged
  claims verify verbatim in the raw text; two rest on an auditor locality error
  and a framing nuance whose content the auditor conceded is true; and one sits
  atop a self-contradictory figure description, where the note follows the
  paper's five separate statements of the effect's direction rather than the
  ambiguous caption. The backfill continued to function as a corpus audit of
  pre-v3 prose: in every case where a legacy field and a newly written v3
  section covered the same fact, the new section was right. Version 0.45.0
  (2026-07-30) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 65 issues 3 and 2 — 26 notes, all v2 augmentations. A backfill adds
  no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 810 v2, and 296 v3 notes. All 26 augmentations
  passed the validator and the mechanical diff-guard on the first attempt with
  no self-fix cycles, and each touched note passed a fresh full independent
  nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 232/234 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with
  zero UNSUPPORTED or CONTRADICTED, after nine evidence-based repairs across
  seven notes in three repair rounds. Issue 2 was the cleanest issue of the
  backfill to date at 116/117 SUPPORTED. Seven of the nine repairs fell on
  legacy prose fields written before the v3 standard, two of them recurrences
  of the documented multi-study support-pattern overstatement (an indirect
  effect said to hold across four studies where one never measured the
  mediator; six hypotheses said to be supported where the paper calls one
  partial), and one an inverted generalizability premise on a paper that argues
  for its setting's transferability. Two repairs touched new v3 fields, with
  unrelated causes. Two residual PARTIAL verdicts are documented rather than
  edited: both are verification artifacts of the interleaved-references
  truncation class, in which a two-column REFERENCES heading sits above
  continuing Limitations and Future Research prose so the strip discards it,
  and both notes' flagged claims verify verbatim in the raw extracted text.
  Version 0.44.0
  (2026-07-30) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 65 issues 5 and 4 — 25 notes, all v2 augmentations. A backfill adds
  no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 836 v2, and 270 v3 notes. The upgrade phase was the
  cleanest of the backfill so far, with all 25 augmentations passing the
  validator and the mechanical diff-guard on the first attempt and no self-fix
  cycles. Each touched note passed a fresh full independent nine-field
  rubric-v2 audit at 218/225 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with zero
  UNSUPPORTED or CONTRADICTED, after fifteen evidence-based repairs across
  thirteen notes in two repair rounds. Thirteen of the fifteen fell on legacy
  prose fields written before the v3 standard. Both documented Mechanism
  Process failure classes appeared again — one note narrated a disconfirmed
  hypothesis as the paper's prediction (Matusik), and two misstated how a
  model is wired (Solomon, Zhang) — while scope drift on Practical
  Implication was the dominant legacy pattern at four instances, each
  addressing prescriptions to audiences the paper never names. Two repairs
  touched new v3 fields, with unrelated causes. Seven residual PARTIAL
  verdicts are documented rather than edited: three are verification
  artifacts from a newly identified truncation class in which a two-column
  REFERENCES heading sits above continuing Discussion prose, so the strip
  discards the interleaved tail; one reproduces a paper's own internal
  discrepancy faithfully; and three are framing nuances on legacy fields
  accepted under the repair convergence bound. In every case where a legacy
  field and a newly written v3 section covered the same fact, the new section
  was correct and the legacy field wrong, so the backfill is also functioning
  as a corpus audit of pre-v3 prose. Version 0.43.0
  (2026-07-29) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 66 issue 1 and volume 65 issue 6 — 26 notes, all v2 augmentations and
  the largest batch of the backfill so far. A backfill adds no papers, so the
  record total is unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier census shifts to 61 v1,
  861 v2, and 245 v3 notes. Each touched note passed a fresh full independent
  nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 228/234 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with
  zero UNSUPPORTED or CONTRADICTED, after thirteen evidence-based repairs
  across eight notes in three repair rounds. Twelve of the thirteen fell on
  legacy prose fields written before the v3 standard, and this is the first
  batch in which both documented Mechanism Process failure classes appeared
  together: three notes misstated what the paper predicted — a disconfirmed
  conditionality narrated as theory (Dimotakis), an explicitly unhypothesized
  claim presented as a prediction (Ong), and a downturn called partially borne
  out that occurred in neither study (Xu) — while two misstated how a model is
  wired (Chan's value-moderating practices, Dwertmann's causal reasoning and
  motive moderation). One repair touched a new v3 field, where recruited-sample
  demographics had been attached to post-exclusion analysed Ns across three
  experiments (Kundro). A second round caught a generalizability caveat the
  paper itself rejects, and a third round found the same premise had propagated
  to an adjacent prose field — a new pattern, since repairing one field left
  the other wrong. Six PARTIAL verdicts are accepted and documented rather than
  edited, because editing accurate content to satisfy a verification artifact
  would itself be a faithfulness failure: three rest on appendices the audit
  tooling trims for context budget, one draws anchored components from a paper
  that states no practical implications, and two are re-scorings of nuances
  that two earlier independent audit rounds had noted and passed. This batch
  ran on claude-opus-5. Earlier, version 0.42.0
  (2026-07-28) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 66 issue 3 and issue 2 — 24 notes, all v2 augmentations. A backfill
  adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 887 v2, and 219 v3 notes. Each touched note passed a
  fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 214/216 prose-field
  verdicts SUPPORTED with zero UNSUPPORTED or CONTRADICTED, after fourteen
  evidence-based repairs across eight notes. Twelve of the fourteen fell on
  legacy prose fields written before the v3 standard, three of them a single
  recurring pattern in which a Mechanism Process misstated how the paper's own
  model is wired — a mediator attributed to the wrong measurement technique
  (Ingram), an above-aspiration effect inverted (Lee), and a dependent variable
  listed as a mediator (Zhang). Two repairs touched new v3 fields, a wrongly
  cited case in Toivonen's Key Findings and a cross-study coverage error in
  Cunningham's Data and Measures; a second round caught two further Data and
  Measures slips, and a third round returned all eighteen affected fields
  SUPPORTED. Two PARTIAL verdicts are accepted and documented rather than
  edited, because editing accurate content to satisfy a verification artifact
  would itself be a faithfulness failure: Hersel's Data and Measures is faithful
  to an appendix the audit tooling trims for context budget, and Toivonen's
  Practical Implication draws anchored components from a paper that states no
  practical implications. This batch ran on claude-opus-5. Earlier, version
  0.41.0 (2026-07-28) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management
  Journal volume 66 issue 5 and issue 4 — 23 notes, all v2 augmentations. A
  backfill
  adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 911 v2, and 195 v3 notes. Each touched note passed a
  fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 207/207 prose-field
  verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED, after ten
  evidence-based repairs across eight notes. Nine of the ten fell on legacy
  prose fields written before the v3 standard, three of them a single recurring
  pattern in which a Mechanism Process presented an empirical outcome as the
  paper's ex ante theory (Banerjee, Lander, Kim); the tenth corrected an
  unstated study country in a new v3 Data and Measures field (Kundro). Nine
  cleared in one repair round and Hussain needed a second for an added-audience
  scope drift, with fresh independent re-audits of every changed note returning
  all nine fields SUPPORTED. This batch ran on claude-opus-5, where backfill
  batches 01 through 07 recorded claude-opus-4-8. Earlier, version 0.40.0
  (2026-07-14) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 67 issue 1 and volume 66 issue 6 — 24 notes, all v2 augmentations. A
  backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the
  version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 934 v2, and 172 v3 notes. Each touched
  note passed a fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 216/216
  prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, or
  CONTRADICTED, after three evidence-based repairs cleared in a single round —
  all three on legacy prose fields written before the v3 standard, each an
  applied-extension scope-drift narrowed back to the paper's own scope: a
  practical implication that had added an unstated platform-designer audience
  (Soublière), a future-research field carrying unframed added directions
  (Park, coevolutionary lock-in), and a limitation asserting a generalizability
  caveat the paper's own Generalizability section argues against (Jia) — each
  re-audited to SUPPORTED. Earlier, version 0.39.0
  (2026-07-12) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 67 issues 3 and 2 — 21 notes, all v2 augmentations. A backfill adds
  no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 958 v2, and 148 v3 notes. Each touched note passed a
  fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 189/189 prose-field
  verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED, after two
  evidence-based repairs cleared in a single round (a Data & Measures
  predecessor/successor count fix on Preston and a legacy-limitations fix
  removing an invented specific from Compagni), each re-audited to SUPPORTED.
  Earlier, version 0.38.0
  (2026-07-12) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 67 issues 5 and 4 — 18 notes, all v2 augmentations. A backfill adds
  no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier
  census shifts to 61 v1, 979 v2, and 127 v3 notes. Each touched note passed a
  fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 162/162 prose-field
  verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED, after
  four evidence-based repairs cleared in a single round (two Data & Measures
  precision fixes on Hallila and Marti, two future-research scope trims on
  Bliese and Madsen), each re-audited to SUPPORTED. Earlier, version 0.37.0
  (2026-07-12) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 68 issue 1 and volume 67 issue 6 — 18 notes, all v2 augmentations. A
  backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the
  version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 997 v2, and 109 v3 notes. Each touched
  note passed a fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2 audit at 160/162
  prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with zero UNSUPPORTED or CONTRADICTED;
  eighteen evidence-based repairs across two rounds narrowed unusually heavy
  legacy scope drift in these issues' practical-implication and future-research
  fields, and two residual PARTIALs (a lightly-extended stated limitation and a
  source-ambiguous, internally-consistent turnover lag) were accepted and
  documented rather than edited. Earlier, version 0.36.0
  (2026-07-11) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 68 issues 3 and 2 — 16 notes, all v2 augmentations (the AMJ v1
  re-extraction tier was cleared in batch 02, so batches 03+ are pure
  augmentation). A backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged
  at 1,167; the version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 1,015 v2, and 91 v3
  notes. Each touched note passed a fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2
  audit at 144/144 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL,
  UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED after two evidence-based scope repairs. Earlier,
  version 0.35.0
  (2026-07-11) continues the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 68 issues 5 and 4 — 19 notes (11 legacy v1 re-extracted, 8 v2
  augmented in place). A backfill adds no papers, so the record total is
  unchanged at 1,167; the version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 1,031 v2, and
  75 v3 notes. Each touched note passed a fresh full independent nine-field
  rubric-v2 audit at 170/171 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with zero
  UNSUPPORTED or CONTRADICTED after five evidence-based repairs; one residual
  PARTIAL remains on a verbatim-faithful mediation figure that two-column
  typesetting splices into the reference list. Earlier, version 0.34.0
  (2026-07-11) begins the v3 backfill of the pre-v3 corpus, upgrading the two
  most recent AMJ issues — volume 69 issue 1 and volume 68 issue 6 (17 notes:
  16 legacy v1 notes fully re-extracted and 1 v2 note augmented in place) — so
  every note in both issues now records hypotheses, data and measures, and key
  findings. A backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at
  1,167; each touched note passed a fresh full independent nine-field rubric-v2
  audit at 153/153 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL,
  UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED after three evidence-based repairs, and the
  version-tier census shifts to 72 v1, 1,039 v2, and 56 v3 notes. Earlier,
  version 0.33.0
  (2026-07-11) adds Academy of Management Journal volume 57, issue 3: 13
  peer-reviewed papers produced under extraction v3 and independently
  audited under rubric v2. One audit-identified field was repaired from PDF
  evidence before release: the Crossland note's list of constructs shown
  empirically distinct from CEO career variety (openness to experience, risk
  propensity, age, and education) had wrongly included CEO tenure. A fresh
  re-audit cleared the repair; the final issue scan has 117/117 prose-field
  verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED. All
  notes validate, the manifest lints cleanly, scoped CrossRef matches every
  changed note, and the public SQLite, CSV, and BibTeX indexes contain 1,167
  records. Earlier, version 0.32.0
  (2026-07-10) adds Academy of Management Journal volume 57, issue 2: 13
  peer-reviewed papers produced under extraction v3 and independently
  audited under rubric v2. Three audit-identified fields were repaired
  from PDF evidence before release: Beckman's board-measure timing,
  Rogan's agency-level robustness qualification, and Wang's
  patent-count-mediated indirect pathway. Fresh re-audits cleared each
  repair; the final issue scan has 117/117 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED
  with zero PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED. All notes validate,
  the manifest lints cleanly, scoped CrossRef matches every changed note,
  and the public SQLite, CSV, and BibTeX indexes contain 1,154 records.
  Earlier, version 0.31.0
  (2026-07-10) adds Academy of Management Journal volume 57, issue 1: 13
  peer-reviewed papers — the first issue produced under extraction v3, so
  every empirical note now records the paper's hypotheses, data and
  measures, and key findings (hypothesis support and effect direction)
  with three additional verbatim evidence anchors, audited under rubric
  v2 across nine prose fields per note. All 13 extractions validated on
  the first attempt and the final audit scan has 117/117 prose-field
  verdicts SUPPORTED with zero PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, or CONTRADICTED.
  The release also fixes a references-stripper bug that could truncate
  audit inputs (with regression tests), raises the audit text budget to
  240,000 characters with anchor-aware splicing so the auditor always
  sees the passages backing each claim, migrates the CrossRef
  false-positive registries to JSON data files, and records truthful
  per-run extraction-model provenance (this issue: claude-fable-5).
  Public indexes contain 1,141 records. Earlier, version 0.30.0
  (2026-07-09) is a schema-and-tooling release with no new notes: it
  introduces extraction v3, which adds three empirical body sections to
  every future note — Hypotheses / Propositions, Data & Measures, and Key
  Findings — plus three matching Layer 1 evidence anchors
  (hypotheses_source, measures_overview, findings_overview) and three new
  Layer 2 audited prose fields under audit rubric v2 (nine fields for v3
  notes; a reversed finding direction is CONTRADICTED). The change is
  applied going-forward only: the validator, auditor, and indexer are
  version-gated on extraction_version, all 1,128 existing v1/v2 notes
  revalidate unchanged, and the rebuilt SQLite and CSV indexes carry the
  three new columns with key_findings and hypotheses now searchable via
  FTS5. The release also adds docs/pipeline-runbook.md, a vendor-neutral
  ingest/audit/publish runbook referenced from AGENTS.md, hardens the
  shared CrossRef client used by all three metadata gates with
  retry-with-backoff and negative caching, and fixes stale documentation
  references. Earlier, version 0.29.0
  (2026-07-07) adds Academy of Management Journal volume 58, issues 1-6:
  78 peer-reviewed papers with issue counts 13, 13, 13, 13, 13, and 13. This
  extends AMJ pilot coverage backward to vol. 58 no. 1 through vol. 69 no. 1,
  and the public SQLite, CSV, and BibTeX indexes now contain 1,128 records.
  The AMJ volume-58 release passes the volume validation stack: all AMJ
  volume-58 manifests lint cleanly, all notes validate, scoped CrossRef
  metadata verification for all 78 AMJ volume-58 notes exits 0 with three
  documented CrossRef-side false positives (Byron title inline-HTML spacing,
  Little / Smith Major author parsing, and Joshi title inline-HTML spacing),
  and the full library has 1,128/1,128 PASS, 0 UNSUPPORTED, and
  0 CONTRADICTED audit verdicts. The final AMJ volume-58 audit scan has
  468/468 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED after six audit-identified prose
  fields were narrowed before release. Earlier, version 0.28.0 (2026-07-05)
  adds Academy of Management Journal volume 59, issues 1-6: 95 peer-reviewed
  papers with issue counts 16, 15, 16, 16, 16, and 16. This extends AMJ pilot
  coverage backward to vol. 59 no. 1 through vol. 69 no. 1, and the public
  SQLite, CSV, and BibTeX indexes now contain 1,050 records. The AMJ
  volume-59 release passes the volume validation stack: all AMJ volume-59
  manifests lint cleanly, all notes validate, scoped CrossRef metadata
